# Any WCH CH340/CH341 USB-serial adapter (idVendor 1a86, idProduct 55d3) gets a
# stable /dev/ch340-<serial> symlink, keyed by the adapter's own serial number
# rather than a role like "left"/"right" -- see examples/06_teleop/README.md's "The udev rule" section
# for why: the same adapter should resolve to the same device path regardless
# of which desk or which arm it is plugged into today, and a calibration file
# keyed by that same serial (see scripts/calibrate_leader_arms.py and
# robosimstudio/robots/teleop/lerobot_controller.py's load_calibration)
# stays correct no matter how the roles get reassigned. One rule, not one per
# unit -- a new adapter just works.
#
# Install:
#   sudo cp scripts/udev/99-ch340-serial.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules && sudo udevadm trigger
#
# Find a plugged-in adapter's serial with:
#   udevadm info -a -n /dev/ttyACM0 | grep -m1 serial
SUBSYSTEM=="tty", ATTRS{idVendor}=="1a86", ATTRS{idProduct}=="55d3", SYMLINK+="ch340-$attr{serial}"
